  },
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "↵It is often difficult to tell how hard developers are working to non-IT folks.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Usually, I try to let them watch Gource.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Setting up Gource on Mac is not difficult, but it has several steps.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "First, you have to have Brew installed.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Then, run the commands below from Terminal,",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The binary will install into /usr/local/bin/gource.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Run the command below to generate the video from a directory with a Git repository↵",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "You can replace the default icon with yours by renaming your avatar to the Git author name such as \"Your Name.png\" as in the Git log, place it in the local directory, and run the Gource command below↵",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "If you feel the video is too long, you can adjust the speed by changing the simulation time scale (default: 1.0) with -c , --time-scale , or SCALE .",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "You can make your video less messy by reducing the maximum number of files from unlimited to a value such as 100 with --max-files NUMBER",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding elasticity is fun with -e 0.5 when a large number of files are being added or deleted.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "More information can be found in Controls",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The video can be output to a file with the option -o FILENAME .",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The file size can be over 10GB for a 1-minute video, so beware.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "After the video is generated, you can use libav to convert it to MP4,↵ ↵Gource of my blog:↵{% youtube iZiZ4CaDkcM %}↵",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "Gsource-on-Mac",
        "title": "Gsource on Mac",
        "url": "/blog/Gsource-on-Mac/"
      }
    }
